1.  Relative delay

    1.  Functions: The following two functions have the same effect, osDelay() and vTaskDelay()

    2.  Timing: It starts counting only from when the function is called until the specified delay time ends

    3.  Call method: Same as the HAL_Delay() method

    ```cpp
    extern "C" //若在C++中运行需要加上该行
    void green_led_task(void const * argument)
    { 
        for(;;) //等同于while(true) 
        { 
        HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_RESET); 
        osDelay(500); 
        HAL_GPIO_WritePin(LED_GPIO_Port, LED_Pin, GPIO_PIN_SET); 
        osDelay(500); 
        }
    }
    ```

2.  Absolute delay

    1.  Functions:

        1.  Get current time: osKernelSysTick()

        2.  Absolute delay function: osDelayUntil()

    2.  Timing: Time starts counting from the beginning of the task; the entire task execution cycle is treated as a whole, suitable for tasks that run at a certain frequency

